---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const articles = [
  {
    id: 'american-center-panel',
    title: 'Equipping educators for a tech-driven future',
    subtitle: 'Insights from the American Center Kampala panel',
    date: 'July 24, 2025',
    readTime: '4 min read',
    tag: 'Field notes',
    body: [
      'Forty educators and technologists met at the American Center Kampala to talk through what classroom technology actually requires from a teacher\'s day. The conversation kept returning to the same point: tech adoption is a school-leadership question before it is a hardware question.',
      'Without an administrator championing a STEM hub inside the school, individual teachers either burn out trying to upgrade alone or quietly revert to chalk and textbook. The room agreed: training programs that don\'t include school heads tend to fail within a term.',
      'Uganda\'s rural schools came up repeatedly. The gap is real, but the framing matters — rural educators don\'t need pity, they need infrastructure parity and a clear pathway from teacher certification through to local mentorship. That\'s what STEMCity\'s programs are designed around.',
    ],
    topics: ['School leadership role', 'Innovation hubs in schools', 'Rural teacher support', 'Tech adoption barriers'],
  },
  {
    id: 'ai-education',
    title: 'Stop racing, start surfing',
    subtitle: 'Rethinking education for an AI-driven future',
    date: 'July 15, 2025',
    readTime: '5 min read',
    tag: null,
    body: [
      'Most of Africa\'s secondary education is still optimised for standardised metrics: memorise, repeat, score, move on. The labour market underneath has already changed shape. The World Economic Forum projects 23% of jobs will look meaningfully different inside five years.',
      'Banning AI in classrooms is a posture that won\'t survive the next two years. The students using it already know more than the policy banning it. The question worth asking instead is what skills cannot be replicated — judgement, ethical reasoning, the capacity to ask the right question — and how to centre those in the curriculum.',
      'For teachers, that means structured time and investment in their own growth. You cannot ask an educator to model adaptive thinking while their week has no slack in it. Teacher development is the precondition for everything else.',
    ],
    topics: ['Labour market shift', 'AI in curriculum', 'Skills that endure', 'Teacher time and investment'],
  },
  {
    id: 'digital-divide',
    title: 'Bridging the digital divide in rural Uganda',
    subtitle: 'What our programs are actually doing',
    date: 'July 10, 2025',
    readTime: '3 min read',
    tag: null,
    body: [
      'The digital divide in rural Uganda is the product of three reinforcing gaps: spotty connectivity, scarce devices, and almost no consistent training pipeline for the teachers expected to use them.',
      'Our work attacks all three. Mobile computer labs reach schools that won\'t have permanent infrastructure for years. Teacher certification programs treat educators as the multipliers they are. Community learning centres let practice continue after the program leaves, and mentorship gives students someone to ask after class.',
      'None of this is novel. The novelty is in running all of it as a connected pipeline rather than as four disconnected pilots that each die at the funding boundary.',
    ],
    topics: ['Mobile labs', 'Teacher certification', 'Community learning centres', 'Mentorship pipeline'],
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="News & field notes — STEMCity Labs"
  description="Short field notes from STEMCity Labs on STEM education, AI in classrooms, civic technology, and bridging the digital divide across East Africa."
>
  <Nav />

  <main>
    <section class="px-6 sm:px-10 pt-8 sm:pt-14 pb-10 sm:pb-12">
      <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-mute mb-5 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="inline-block w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-brand"></span>
        News & field notes
      </p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-medium leading-[1.04] tracking-[-0.025em] max-w-4xl">
        Short notes from the work — <em class="text-brand italic">what we're learning as we go.</em>
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft max-w-2xl">
        Quick reads on STEM education, AI in classrooms, civic technology, and bridging the digital divide. Each one a self-contained note, not a teaser for something longer.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="px-6 sm:px-10 py-8 sm:py-12 border-t border-ink/10">
      <div class="grid gap-4">
        {articles.map((a) => (
          <article id={a.id} class="p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl border border-ink/10 hover:border-brand/40 hover:bg-brand/[0.02] transition scroll-mt-20">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 flex-wrap mb-4">
              {a.tag && (
                <span class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-brand text-paper">{a.tag}</span>
              )}
              <span class="font-mono text-[11px] text-mute tracking-[0.06em]">{a.date}</span>
              <span class="font-mono text-[11px] text-mute tracking-[0.06em]">·</span>
              <span class="font-mono text-[11px] text-mute tracking-[0.06em]">{a.readTime}</span>
            </div>
            <h2 class="font-display text-xl sm:text-2xl font-medium tracking-[-0.015em] leading-tight max-w-3xl">{a.title}</h2>
            <p class="font-display text-base sm:text-lg text-brand italic mt-2 max-w-2xl">{a.subtitle}</p>
            <div class="mt-5 max-w-2xl space-y-4 text-base text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
              {a.body.map((p) => <p>{p}</p>)}
            </div>
            <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-mute mt-6 mb-3">In this note</p>
            <ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
              {a.topics.map((t) => (
                <li class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-ink/5 text-xs">
                  <span class="w-1 h-1 rounded-full bg-mute"></span>
                  {t}
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-brand text-brand-ink px-6 sm:px-10 py-8 sm:py-12">
      <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 items-center">
        <div class="lg:col-span-7">
          <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-brand-deep mb-3">Newsletter</p>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl sm:text-2xl font-medium tracking-[-0.025em] leading-tight">Field notes in your inbox, every couple of weeks.</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-brand-deep">No padding, no roundups, just what we're learning.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="lg:col-span-5">
          <form class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-2">
            <input type="email" required placeholder="you@example.com" class="flex-1 px-4 py-3 rounded-full bg-paper text-ink placeholder:text-mute focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-ink/20 text-sm" />
            <button type="submit" class="text-sm font-medium px-5 py-3 bg-ink text-paper rounded-full hover:bg-brand-ink transition inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-1.5">
              Subscribe <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </button>
          </form>
          <p class="font-mono text-[10px] text-brand-deep mt-2 tracking-wider">Signup wiring in progress — for now, email <a href="mailto:stemcitylabs@gmail.com" class="underline hover:no-underline">stemcitylabs@gmail.com</a> with "subscribe" in the subject.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
